WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.169 --> 00:00:05.929
All right, so now that we have our player pawn set up

2
00:00:05.929 --> 00:00:09.429
to actually receive a score and a time pickup,

3
00:00:09.429 --> 00:00:11.609
it's now actually time to create that pickup.

4
00:00:11.609 --> 00:00:13.410
And we're gonna be doing this

5
00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:16.710
by first creating a new blueprint

6
00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:19.469
and using actor as the parent class.

7
00:00:19.469 --> 00:00:21.730
Let's just pop over into the editor,

8
00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:25.129
hit control space to bring up my content browser.

9
00:00:25.129 --> 00:00:27.649
And then I'm gonna come again up to my content folder,

10
00:00:27.649 --> 00:00:30.570
just gonna right click in here, blueprint class,

11
00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:32.850
and then base this off of actor.

12
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:39.929
I'm gonna call this BP underscore pickup.

13
00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:41.869
Once we have done that,

14
00:00:41.869 --> 00:00:44.130
the next thing that we're going to do

15
00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:47.090
is we are going to open up our blueprint

16
00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:50.570
and add a sphere collision in a static mesh.

17
00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:53.530
And we're gonna set the static mesh shape to Taurus.

18
00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:55.649
So let's go ahead and do that now.

19
00:00:55.649 --> 00:00:56.869
So again, we're gonna come here,

20
00:00:56.869 --> 00:00:59.439
we're gonna open up our BP pickup.

21
00:00:59.439 --> 00:01:00.960
And then on the components,

22
00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.439
we're gonna click on this add

23
00:01:03.079 --> 00:01:07.349
and we're gonna look for a sphere collision, okay?

24
00:01:07.349 --> 00:01:10.069
And then we're gonna click on add again,

25
00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:15.489
and we're gonna look for a static mesh, there we go.

26
00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:18.530
Then for our static mesh, I'm gonna come over here

27
00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:22.010
and we're gonna look for a, I don't know,

28
00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:24.650
let's just use this arcade sphere right here.

29
00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.549
And I think that's actually a little bit too big.

30
00:01:26.549 --> 00:01:30.090
So what we're gonna do is I come here to the scale

31
00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:35.730
and I'm just gonna 0.25, maybe 0.1.

32
00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:36.650
Yeah, there we go, that works.

33
00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:39.209
So 0.1, scale that down a little bit.

34
00:01:39.209 --> 00:01:41.129
So that is perfect.

35
00:01:41.129 --> 00:01:43.799
Now, the next thing that we need to do

36
00:01:43.799 --> 00:01:47.040
is we are going to select our sphere

37
00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.980
and then we're going to go to the events

38
00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:52.519
and we're gonna press the on component begin overlap.

39
00:01:52.519 --> 00:01:54.159
What this is gonna do is this is going

40
00:01:54.159 --> 00:01:56.939
to automatically create an event for us

41
00:01:56.939 --> 00:01:58.599
that is going to fire off

42
00:01:58.599 --> 00:02:02.799
once something has begin to overlap this component.

43
00:02:02.799 --> 00:02:06.760
So very simply, we're gonna grab this sphere right here,

44
00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.360
our sphere collision, I'm gonna scroll down

45
00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.960
and keep on going right here to our events.

46
00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:14.159
I'm gonna say this on component begin overlap.

47
00:02:14.159 --> 00:02:16.280
I'm gonna press this plus sign right here,

48
00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:18.659
which is gonna kick us over to the event graph,

49
00:02:18.659 --> 00:02:19.639
adding to that node

50
00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:23.530
and then focusing us right there on that node.

51
00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:25.009
Now with that node added,

52
00:02:25.009 --> 00:02:27.449
the next thing that we need to do

53
00:02:27.449 --> 00:02:30.490
is we're gonna do a check to make sure

54
00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:32.770
that the item that we're running over

55
00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:34.930
does implement our interface.

56
00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:39.129
And then if we do, we are going to basically make a call

57
00:02:39.129 --> 00:02:41.449
and then set our score and our time.

58
00:02:41.449 --> 00:02:44.090
Now, the reason that we're making sure

59
00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:47.169
that when we overlap this particular actor

60
00:02:47.169 --> 00:02:49.289
that it implements our interface,

61
00:02:49.289 --> 00:02:51.610
it could be very easy

62
00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:55.030
that you have a player pawn or an AI pawn

63
00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:58.229
and you don't want the AI pawn to interact with this,

64
00:02:58.229 --> 00:03:00.310
you only want the player or maybe you don't.

65
00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:01.990
In our case, we only want the player.

66
00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:03.469
So we do wanna make sure

67
00:03:03.469 --> 00:03:06.509
that whatever interacts with this pickup object,

68
00:03:06.509 --> 00:03:08.990
that it does have our interface in it.

69
00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:12.030
So to do this, we're gonna come here

70
00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:15.750
and we are going to first off of our other actors,

71
00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.960
we're gonna look for does

72
00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.520
and then right there does implement interface.

73
00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:23.039
And the interface that we're gonna be checking for

74
00:03:23.039 --> 00:03:25.520
is our, if I just type in BPI,

75
00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:28.960
we're gonna find it right there, a BPI stats interface.

76
00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:30.319
Then what we're gonna do

77
00:03:30.319 --> 00:03:33.280
is this is returning a Boolean values.

78
00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.280
Remember Booleans are true or false.

79
00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.370
So we're gonna look for a branch

80
00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:40.490
and then under utilities flow control,

81
00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:41.629
we're gonna add a branch.

82
00:03:41.629 --> 00:03:42.889
You can also add a branch quickly

83
00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:45.770
by pressing the B key on the keyboard and left clicking

84
00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:47.889
that will add the branch node as well.

85
00:03:47.889 --> 00:03:49.650
And with our branch added,

86
00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:52.650
what I'm gonna do is I'm gonna connect the execution

87
00:03:52.689 --> 00:03:55.409
of our on component begin overlap

88
00:03:55.409 --> 00:03:56.930
to the input on our branch.

89
00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:59.090
Oops, missed that input, there we go.

90
00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:02.530
And again, I only want this to fire off

91
00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:04.569
if we do implement that interface.

92
00:04:04.569 --> 00:04:06.490
So I'm gonna take the return value

93
00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:08.090
from our does implement interface

94
00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:09.650
and plug that into our condition.

95
00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:12.650
And this is gonna make us a check.

96
00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:14.069
Next, what we're gonna do

97
00:04:14.069 --> 00:04:16.170
is we're gonna pull off of the true here

98
00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:18.730
because we want to make sure that when this is true,

99
00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.290
we actually do something

100
00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:23.860
and we're gonna go pick up object

101
00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.600
and we want this message.

102
00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:28.779
So the message is going to allow us to basically say,

103
00:04:28.779 --> 00:04:30.800
hey, I have received this,

104
00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:32.480
what do you want me to do with it?

105
00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:34.860
And for us, what we're gonna do here

106
00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:35.860
is first things first,

107
00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:37.699
we're gonna take this other actor

108
00:04:37.699 --> 00:04:39.860
and we're gonna plug this into target.

109
00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:43.019
This is just ensuring that we are actually working

110
00:04:43.019 --> 00:04:46.180
on the correct and with the correct interface,

111
00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:48.300
I'm also adding to reroute nodes

112
00:04:48.339 --> 00:04:51.459
to make it a little bit easier just to read this graph.

113
00:04:51.459 --> 00:04:53.720
Now, this score and time pickup

114
00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:55.839
is gonna be something that is placeable

115
00:04:55.839 --> 00:04:58.500
by a level designer or level artist.

116
00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:01.319
So next thing that we're gonna do

117
00:05:01.319 --> 00:05:05.300
is we are going to expose some parameters,

118
00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:08.040
more specifically for our score and time,

119
00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:11.100
we are gonna make these both instance edible.

120
00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:13.839
So to do that, this is really, really simple.

121
00:05:13.839 --> 00:05:15.860
What we're gonna do is we're just gonna right click

122
00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:17.939
on the score and promote to variable

123
00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:19.920
and then I'm gonna pull this down like so,

124
00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.540
and then do the same thing for the time,

125
00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:22.980
promote to variable,

126
00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:25.060
and I'm gonna pull this one down as well.

127
00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:27.720
So I'm gonna just stack these right over here.

128
00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:31.199
Now I do need to compile and save this, there we go.

129
00:05:31.199 --> 00:05:33.480
And last but not least, again,

130
00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:34.959
I want these to be editable

131
00:05:34.959 --> 00:05:37.139
when this is placed inside of a level.

132
00:05:37.139 --> 00:05:38.540
So to do that, we're gonna come here

133
00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:41.139
and we're gonna make these variables public

134
00:05:41.139 --> 00:05:43.579
by pressing this little I right here,

135
00:05:43.579 --> 00:05:45.000
it will now be editable

136
00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:48.480
once we have placed it inside of our level.

137
00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.079
So we're gonna go ahead and save.

138
00:05:50.079 --> 00:05:52.420
And the last thing that we need to do with this

139
00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:55.199
is we're gonna add this destroy actor.

140
00:05:55.199 --> 00:05:58.319
Now what this will do is this will destroy this actor

141
00:05:58.319 --> 00:06:01.040
or remove it from the gameplay level

142
00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:03.000
once we have finished.

143
00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.560
So let's go ahead and do that now.

144
00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:05.959
So we're gonna come here

145
00:06:05.959 --> 00:06:08.680
and we are going to just drag off of this

146
00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:12.980
and look for destroy and there's our destroy actor.

147
00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:15.269
So again, just to recap,

148
00:06:15.269 --> 00:06:20.269
we first added our sphere and our sphere collision, okay?

149
00:06:20.589 --> 00:06:24.550
And then we shrunk our sphere down to a point one

150
00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:25.889
because it's a little bit small.

151
00:06:25.889 --> 00:06:27.689
We then grabbed our sphere right here

152
00:06:27.689 --> 00:06:29.110
and then in our details panel,

153
00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:32.459
we came over and on component begin overlap

154
00:06:32.459 --> 00:06:34.420
was added to our event graph.

155
00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:36.180
We then check to see if the component

156
00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:38.379
or the object that we're overlapping

157
00:06:38.379 --> 00:06:40.879
has our interface and if it does,

158
00:06:40.879 --> 00:06:44.680
we are then gonna make a call to give a default score

159
00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:47.079
and a default amount of time.

160
00:06:47.079 --> 00:06:48.800
And then we're gonna destroy this.

161
00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:50.879
The last thing that we need to do here

162
00:06:50.879 --> 00:06:54.459
for our integer and our time, our score and our time,

163
00:06:54.459 --> 00:06:58.139
I'm just gonna set the default values of these to five.

164
00:06:58.139 --> 00:06:59.959
We don't necessarily need to do this

165
00:06:59.959 --> 00:07:03.040
but with everything that we have going on at one time,

166
00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:05.240
this will make sure that once we go to test this,

167
00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:07.759
things will work and then we're not sitting there stuck

168
00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:10.920
scratching our heads wondering why something isn't working.

169
00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:13.959
So this does it for this particular section

170
00:07:13.959 --> 00:07:16.120
of our video tutorial series.

171
